Planet Venus – Feed Aggregator:
Planet Venus is a powerful and flexible “river of news” feed reader and aggregator.
It fetches news feeds (RSS, Atom, RDF, CDF) from multiple websites, merges them, and produces a single unified feed — latest updates first.

Features:
Aggregates multiple feed formats: RSS, Atom, RDF, CDF
Cleans and corrects malformed markup using BeautifulSoup
Generates static output with customizable templates via XSLT or templating engines
Produces a “river of news” format — ideal for community news portals or blog aggregators
Lightweight and easy to configure

Planet Venus uses:
Universal Feed Parser – for parsing diverse feed formats
BeautifulSoup – for handling invalid HTML/XML
XSLT / Custom Templates – for flexible output generation

Install dependencies:
pip install feedparser beautifulsoup4

Installation
Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/gentoo/venus.git
cd venus

View the documentation:
open docs/index.html

Create a configuration file:
cp examples/config.ini myplanet.ini
Your aggregated feed will be generated in the output directory you specified.
